# autotune-usb: Auto Tune multimode (issue #205) SUGGESTING a gross alignment in
# USB - and NOT moving the dial.
#
# This is the fixture of the rule that matters most in SSB: a voice signal has no
# carrier and no absolute pitch reference, so the assistant only estimates the
# coarse alignment of the occupied energy inside the sideband and *asks*. The
# APP 6 "Auto Tune" button is pressed once and the session goes COLLECT (five
# consistent frames) -> PREVIEW: the dial has to be EXACTLY where it was.
#
# scenario_settle arms a TEST-ONLY voice mass centred 2850 Hz above the dial
# (mocks/mock_dsp.c), i.e. mostly outside the 300..2700 Hz passband of the USB
# filter, so the best discrete shift is +752 Hz (|d| <= 800 Hz, step 188 Hz).
# The fixture then advances the virtual clock past the 3000 ms COLLECT window:
# a session that is still alive AND has not moved the dial after that can only be
# in PREVIEW (the collect timeout ends the session; the preview expiry is 5000 ms
# and this fixture stays inside it).
#
# What the fixture *means*: "suggested, not tuned". Retuning the voice without
# the operator's second press would move the dial in the capture and be a failure;
# so would a session that timed out instead of producing a suggestion. The real
# USB/LSB voice with a 500 Hz shift, and the two-QSO abstention, are the owner's
# radio (docs/autotune.md).

name autotune-usb
screen autotune-usb

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 96000

mode usb
filter_low 0
filter_high 3000
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
